current_state.mode == "GUIDED"`). When the user presses SPACE, controlMode = MODE_HOVER_CUSTOM, which runs the PD+DOB attitude control loop publishing AttitudeTarget to /mavros/setpoint_raw/attitude.

So
[/THINK]
[2026-08-05T07:43:49.037Z] [THINK]
 for ground_station.py, the DOB hover should:
1. When hover is requested, switch control from velocity publishing to DOB hover: publish AttitudeTarget on /mavros/setpoint_raw/attitude.
2. It needs pose (already subscribed
[/THINK]
[2026-08-05T07:43:49.454Z] [THINK]
: /mavros/local_position/pose) and velocity (need to add: /mavros/local_position/velocity_local — note C++ uses velocity_local when not using odin).
3. Grab target position at hover start (current position +
[/THINK]
[2026-08-05T07:43:49.866Z] [THINK]
 yaw), then run the PD+DOB loop:
   - err = target - pos
   - Kp_xy = wn_xy², Kd_xy = 2ζ·wn_xy
   - target_acc_pid = Kp·err − Kd·vel
[/THINK]
[2026-08-05T07:43:50.280Z] [THINK]

   - DOB low-pass observer: z = z/(L·dt+1) − L²·dt·vel/(L·dt+1) − L·u·dt/(L·dt+1); d_hat = z + L·vel
   - u = target
[/THINK]
[2026-08-05T07:43:50.719Z] [THINK]
_acc_pid − d_hat
   - accel_total = u + gravity
   - quaternion from accel direction and yaw_des
   - thrust = hover_throttle-based mapping
   - publish AttitudeTarget

Also, the gain parameters: "复用对应的增益参数" — reuse the same gain parameters. The C++ reads them from YAML
[/THINK]
